.venv-sandbox/

# Key material must never reach the repo, and the broker path creates some.
# signer.py's make_signer writes a generated P-256 private key to disk on first
# use, and the enrollment flow leaves a broker state file beside it. Neither was
# ignored, so a clean-machine bring-up that exercised the broker left a private
# key sitting in `git status` as an untracked file, one `git add -A` away from
# being committed. .vercelignore carries a matching *.pem rule so a laptop-run
# `vercel --prod`, which uploads the working directory rather than the committed
# tree, cannot ship one either.
keys/
*.pem
*.broker-state.json
